  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISS, East Africa Peace and Security Governance Programme (EPSG), 2022 - 2025 - ISS, East Africa Peace and Security Governance Programme (EPSG)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ISS, East Africa Peace and Security Governance Programme (EPSG), 2022 - 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ISS Nairobi Office, through the East African Peace and Security Governance (EPSG) programme, will seek to expand and deepen its strategic presence and engagement in Kenya, Eastern Africa and the Great Lakes region. ISS intends to work with selected governments in East Africa and subregional organizations such as the EAC and ICGLR. The programme &quot;Strengthening regional capacities for conflict prevention, peacebuilding, the rule of law and democratic governance in Eastern Africa (including the Great Lakes)&quot; is focused on contributing to two strategic outcomes:

1. Enhanced knowledge and understanding of threats to peace and security in East Africa and the Great Lakes among relevant regional stakeholders.

2. Improved national and regional cooperative capacities to address threats to peace and security, prevent conflict and enhance community security.

The planned budget is SEK 14 million SEK over three years.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Institute of Security Studies ska genomf&#xf6;ra ett projekt f&#xf6;r att &#x201d;st&#xe4;rka regionala kapaciteter f&#xf6;r konfliktf&#xf6;rebyggande, fredsbyggande, r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen och demokratiskt styre i &#xf6;stra Afrika (inklusive Stora Sj&#xf6;-omr&#xe5;det)&#x201d; under perioden december 2022 &#x2013; november 2025 som en del av deras program f&#xf6;r freds- och s&#xe4;kerhetsstyrning i &#xd6;stafrika. Sidas st&#xf6;d uppg&#xe5;r till 14,4 miljoner kronor. Projektet syftar till att bidra till tv&#xe5; strategiska resultat:
1. F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad kunskap och f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else f&#xf6;r hot mot fred och s&#xe4;kerhet i &#xd6;stafrika och de stora sj&#xf6;arna bland relevanta regionala intressenter.
2. F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad nationell och regional samarbetskapacitet f&#xf6;r att hantera hot mot fred och s&#xe4;kerhet, f&#xf6;rebygga konflikter och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra s&#xe4;kerheten i samh&#xe4;llet. 
ISS avser att arbeta med utvalda regeringar i &#xd6;stafrika och subregionala organisationer som EAC och ICGLR. Tematiska fokusomr&#xe5;den &#xe4;r konfliktf&#xf6;rebyggande, fredsbyggande, fr&#xe4;mjande av demokratiskt styre och r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Institute of Security Studies will implement a project to &#x201c;Strengthening regional capacities for conflict prevention, peacebuilding, the rule of law and democratic governance in Eastern Africa (including the Great Lakes region)&#x201d; for the period December 2022 &#x2013; November 2025 as part of their East Africa Peace and Security Governance Programme. Sida&#x2019;s support amounts to SEK 14,4 million SEK. The project aims to contribute towards two strategic outcomes:

1.	Enhanced knowledge and understanding of threats to peace and security in East Africa and the Great Lakes among relevant regional stakeholders.
2.	Improved national and regional cooperative capacities to address threats to peace and security, prevent conflict and enhance community security.

ISS intends to work with selected governments in East Africa and subregional organizations such as the EAC and ICGLR. Thematic areas of focus are conflict prevention, peacebuilding, promoting democratic governance and rule of law.</narrative>
  </description>
